Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was a NullPointerException (NPE) occurring during the comparison of action end times for nodes in a workflow instance when rerunning workflows that involve forks. The original code initialized the comparison dates (`date1` and `date2`) to a constant value (`FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE`), which could lead to incorrect comparisons if the corresponding node instances were not found. The patch modified the code to initialize these dates to `null` and then set them to `FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE` only if they remained `null` after attempting to retrieve the action end times. This change ensures that the comparison logic handles missing node instances correctly, preventing the NPE.
